# ev.rules — contextual dialogue for ENDEARING VOID
# After Elan Ruskin's GDC 2012 "AI-driven Dynamic Dialog" (Valve response rules).
#
# Edit this file, press F6 in-game to hot reload. No recompile.
#
# FORMAT
#   rule <name>            start a rule (name shows in the log)
#   who <speaker>          gibbons | narrator (narrator = unattributed line)
#   criteria k=v k<n ...   ALL must be true. Ops: = < <= > >= and a..b ranges.
#                          A criterion naming a fact absent from the query FAILS.
#                          More criteria = more specific = wins over general rules.
#   say "..."              response line. Repeat for variants; one is chosen at
#                          random, cycling so all are heard before any repeats.
#   remember k=v k+=1      write memory when the rule fires. @N = expires in N sec.
#   then <who> <concept> after <sec>   chain a followup query when the line ends.
#                          Re-queried at fire time — if the world changed, silence.
#   norepeat               rule disables itself after firing once.
#   resay <sec>            cooldown before this rule may fire again.
#   end                    close the rule.
#
# FACTS AVAILABLE (dialog_game.c adds more as needed — ask for anything):
#   concept                waypoint | idle | <any concept a "then" clause names>
#   who                    speaker being queried
#   scene                  space_lobby, space_corridor, space_suite, glasshouse,
#                          balcony, lobby, elevator, taxi... (state_names table)
#   scene_time total_time  seconds
#   waypoint               Gibbons' current waypoint index (when he's active)
#   gibbons_dist           metres from player to Gibbons
#   gibbons_behavior       walking | waiting | reading | sitting | gazing | gesturing
#   tasks_done             suite ritual progress 0..4
#   lobby_visits           space lobby entry count
#   backstory_count        taxi/title choices answered 0..6
#   player_speed player_still random(0..99)
#   window_revealed phone_ringing   (suite only)
#   ...plus anything a rule remembered.

# ══ SPACE LOBBY — the tour ═══════════════════════════════════════════
# First visit: baseline rules. Return visit (backstory_count>3) adds one
# criterion, scores higher, and quietly replaces every line.

rule sl_tour_ready
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_lobby waypoint=0
say "The room's been ready for some time."
remember met_gibbons=1
end

rule sl_tour_time
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_lobby waypoint=1
say "Take your time."
end

rule sl_tour_thisway
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_lobby waypoint=2
say "This way."
end

rule sl_tour_nearby
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_lobby waypoint=3
say "I'll be nearby."
then gibbons lobby_aside after 2.5
end

# The aside only lands if the player is still standing there when the line
# ends — walk away and the conversation self-terminates. (Slide 79.)
rule sl_aside_lingering
who gibbons
criteria concept=lobby_aside scene=space_lobby player_still=1 gibbons_dist<6
say "Most guests head straight through. No shame in lingering."
norepeat
end

# ── Return visit — one extra criterion, so these win when true ──
rule sl_return_ready
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_lobby waypoint=0 backstory_count>3
say "I thought you might come back."
end

rule sl_return_window
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_lobby waypoint=1 backstory_count>3
say "The window hasn't moved."
end

rule sl_return_corridor
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_lobby waypoint=2 backstory_count>3
say "Same corridor. Shorter this time."
end

rule sl_return_findme
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_lobby waypoint=3 backstory_count>3
say "You know where to find me."
end

# ══ SPACE CORRIDOR — the walk to the suite ═══════════════════════════

rule corr_nocturne
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_corridor waypoint=0
say "Someone in Four plays that same nocturne every evening."
end

rule corr_gentleman
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_corridor waypoint=1
say "The gentleman in Six orders for two. Every night. Sends half back."
end

rule corr_yours
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_corridor waypoint=2
say "Yours is at the end. I left the curtains open."
end

# Return visit — the corridor's stories have endings now.
rule corr_return_nocturne
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_corridor waypoint=0 backstory_count>3
say "Four stopped playing last week. Nobody noticed."
end

rule corr_return_gentleman
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_corridor waypoint=1 backstory_count>3
say "Six checked out. The trays stopped coming."
end

rule corr_return_yours
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=space_corridor waypoint=2 backstory_count>3
say "Yours is as you left it."
end

# ══ GLASSHOUSE — the observation lounge ══════════════════════════════
# Return visit says one thing at the first stop, then lets the room talk.

rule gh_lounge
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=glasshouse waypoint=0
say "The observation lounge. Most guests spend the evening here."
end

rule gh_through
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=glasshouse waypoint=1
say "Your suite is just through."
end

rule gh_return_quieter
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=glasshouse waypoint=0 backstory_count>3
say "Quieter tonight."
end

# Return visit, second stop — the extra criterion outranks the tour line.
rule gh_return_through
who gibbons
criteria concept=waypoint scene=glasshouse waypoint=1 backstory_count>3
say "You remember the way."
end

# ══ SUITE PROPS — concept=interact, object=<name>, step=N ════════════
# Every E-press tags its prop; the database decides if there's a line.
# SILENT BY DESIGN (architecture speaks — do not add rules): adjoining_door,
# wardrobe, photograph, sock, suitcase, bathroom, lamp, desk, bed, champagne.

rule int_thermostat
who gibbons
criteria concept=interact object=thermostat step=1
say "It's set where it's set for a reason, sir."
resay 60
end

# Keep cycling it and he notices — step counts around the dial.
rule int_thermostat_fiddling
who gibbons
criteria concept=interact object=thermostat step>=3
say "It goes around, sir. That's all it does."
norepeat
end

rule int_book
who gibbons
criteria concept=interact object=book step=1
say "The previous guest left it. Or we provide them. I forget which."
end

rule int_wineglass
who gibbons
criteria concept=interact object=wineglass step=1
say "One glass. We notice these things. We don't mention them."
remember saw_glass=1
then gibbons wineglass_beat after 2.0
end

# Only lands if the player is still standing with the glass when the
# line ends. Walk away and he keeps it to himself.
rule int_wineglass_beat
who gibbons
criteria concept=wineglass_beat scene=space_suite player_still=1
say "I'll bring another up. In case."
norepeat
end

rule int_postcard
who gibbons
criteria concept=interact object=postcard step=1
say "There's a mailbox in the lobby. The rates are optimistic."
end

rule int_roomservice
who gibbons
criteria concept=interact object=roomservice step=1
say "The kitchen never closes. There's no night up here to close for."
end

rule int_phone
who gibbons
criteria concept=interact object=phone step=1
say "For the room, mostly. Occasionally the front desk. Never further."
remember touched_phone=1
end

# ══ IDLE — ambient observations, polled every ~10s ═══════════════════
# random<N keeps them scarce. resay keeps them from cycling too fast.
# Silence is the default answer; these are exceptions to it.

rule idle_lobby_smalltalk
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=space_lobby random<25
say "Gravity here is point nine. Nobody complains."
say "The elevator takes eleven minutes. I've timed it."
remember lobby_idles+=1
resay 30
end

# Running gag: after he's made two observations, a more specific rule
# (one extra criterion — 5 beats smalltalk's 4) takes over — once.
rule idle_lobby_threehours
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=space_lobby lobby_idles>=2 met_gibbons=1
say "Still three hours to kill, sir."
norepeat
end

rule idle_corridor
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=space_corridor random<25
say "The corridor is longer than it needs to be. By design, I'm told."
say "The carpet is new. It won't be."
resay 45
end

rule idle_glasshouse_gazing
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=glasshouse gibbons_behavior=gazing
say "It's rude to stare. The Earth doesn't mind."
norepeat
end

rule idle_suite_warming
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=space_suite tasks_done>=3 random<40
say "The room warms up when it's used. Like anything."
norepeat
end

rule idle_suite_phone
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=space_suite phone_ringing=1
say "You could answer that. Or not. It stops eventually."
resay 20
end

# Narrator speaks where Gibbons doesn't go.
rule idle_balcony_city
who narrator
criteria concept=idle scene=balcony random<20 scene_time>25
say "The city doesn't know you're up here."
norepeat
end

# ══ THE BED — ending permutations (concept=enter, scene=bed) ═════════
# The Vanaman principle (TWD ending): one beat, recontextualized by the
# player's accumulated history. Every permutation must read as a valid
# EV story — general baseline, increasingly specific exceptions.
# The narrator speaks unattributed. One line only. Then the music.

rule end_bed_base
who narrator
criteria concept=enter scene=bed
say "Three hours. Nearly done."
norepeat
end

rule end_bed_untouched
who narrator
criteria concept=enter scene=bed tasks_done<1
say "You lie down in a room that never learned your name."
norepeat
end

rule end_bed_ritual
who narrator
criteria concept=enter scene=bed tasks_done>=4
say "The room is warm. You did everything two people would have done."
norepeat
end

rule end_bed_photo
who narrator
criteria concept=enter scene=bed photograph_flipped=1
say "The photograph is face-up on the nightstand. You can't see it from here. You know."
norepeat
end

# Most specific: full ritual AND you turned her over. Scores 6.
rule end_bed_photo_ritual
who narrator
criteria concept=enter scene=bed tasks_done>=4 photograph_flipped=1
say "The room is warm, and Paris is face-up in the dark. You did the whole evening for two. Both of you were here, in a way."
norepeat
end

# You met the glass and did nothing else — the quietest permutation.
rule end_bed_glass
who narrator
criteria concept=enter scene=bed saw_glass=1 tasks_done<2
say "One glass, still out. Somebody should put it away. Not tonight."
norepeat
end

# ══ CARRY REACTIONS — the boombox move ═══════════════════════════════
# Facts: holding=1 while carrying anything; carrying=<tag> for named props
# (guest_register, vase, ashtray, coffee_cup, photograph, postcard,
# pillow_red, pillow_blue, her_book). Fired by the idle poll — pick a thing
# up and keep walking; the world notices. Most carries stay silent.

# Amalfitano's geometry book on the washing line (2666). She left it;
# carry it to the balcony and the game knows exactly what you're doing.
rule carry_book_balcony
who narrator
criteria concept=idle scene=balcony carrying=her_book
say "Hang it on the railing. See what it learns out here."
norepeat
end

rule carry_book_suite
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=space_suite carrying=her_book random<60
say "Geometry. The previous... it was left, sir. It's yours if you want it."
norepeat
end

# The photograph, carried instead of faced — devastating politeness.
rule carry_photograph
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=space_suite carrying=photograph
say "I can have a frame sent up."
norepeat
end

# The ashtray that shouldn't exist — Puzzle Agent beat.
rule carry_ashtray
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=lobby carrying=ashtray
say "That shouldn't be here at all. Take it. I saw nothing."
norepeat
end

# Her pillow. He says the kindest possible nothing-much.
rule carry_pillow_blue
who gibbons
criteria concept=idle scene=space_suite carrying=pillow_blue
say "Housekeeping can restore the arrangement, sir. Or not."
norepeat
end
